# 1. Why Monitor EKS?

A production Kubernetes cluster contains many components:

```text id="n1y7r4"
Users

 |

Load Balancer

 |

Ingress

 |

Services

 |

Pods

 |

Containers

 |

Worker Nodes

 |

AWS Infrastructure
```

Problems can happen anywhere:

* Application errors
* High CPU usage
* Memory exhaustion
* Node failures
* Network issues
* Storage failures

Monitoring helps answer:

* Is the application healthy?
* Are users experiencing failures?
* Which component is causing problems?
* When did the issue start?

